            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Bog Rot"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(curse, disease, divine, necromancy, negative)\n\nThis affliction can't be reduced below stage 1, nor can the damage from it be healed, until it's successfully treated with remove curse or a similar effect; the affliction can then be removed as normal for a disease. A creature killed by bog rot melts into a noxious sludge and can't be resurrected except by a 7th-level resurrect ritual or similar magic\n\nDC 21 Fortitude; Stage 1: carrier with no ill effect (1 minute); Stage 2: 3d6 negative damage and clumsy 1 (1 day)"
            },
